format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: radioactivity

objective u2-half-life-meaning
statement: Know that half-life is the time for about half of a large group of radioactive nuclei to decay.
misconception: A radioactive atom is half gone after one half-life.

item u2-l3-choice-left
type: choice
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-21-3

prompt:
    A sample has gone through one half-life. Which statement is true?

options:
    {"id":"about","label":"About half of the nuclei have decayed, and the rest were not cut in half"}
    {"id":"each","label":"Every nucleus has lost half of itself","note":"Nuclei are not cut in half. About half of them have decayed and the others have not changed."}
    {"id":"weaker","label":"Every nucleus is now half as radioactive","note":"Each nucleus is either still unstable or has already changed."}

answer: about

explanation:
    About half of the nuclei have decayed. The rest were not cut in half.

item u2-l3-choice-meaning
type: choice
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-21-3

prompt:
    What does half-life mean?

options:
    {"id":"group","label":"The time for about half of a large group of nuclei to decay"}
    {"id":"one","label":"The time for one atom to decay","note":"Half-life describes a group, not one atom."}
    {"id":"half","label":"The time for each atom to lose half of itself","note":"Atoms are not cut in half. About half of the nuclei have decayed."}
    {"id":"gone","label":"The time until the sample is no longer radioactive","note":"Some radioactivity is still there after one half-life."}

answer: group

explanation:
    Half-life is the time for about half of a large group of radioactive nuclei to decay.

item u2-l3-predict-hundred
type: predict
surfaces: lesson

prompt:
    There are 100 radioactive nuclei. After one half-life, what happens?

input: choice

options:
    {"id":"one","label":"One nucleus disappears"}
    {"id":"half","label":"Every atom becomes half as radioactive"}
    {"id":"about-half","label":"About half of the nuclei have decayed"}
    {"id":"gone","label":"All the radioactivity is gone"}

answer: about-half

explanation:
    Your guess is not scored. The answer comes later in the lesson.

item u2-x-fill-half
type: fill
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-21-3

prompt:
    Half-life is the time for about ___ of a large group of nuclei to decay.

mode: bank

bank:
    {"id":"half","label":"half"}
    {"id":"all","label":"all"}
    {"id":"tenth","label":"a tenth"}

answer: half

explanation:
    Half-life is the time for about half of a large group of radioactive nuclei to decay.

item u2-x-half-best
type: choice
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-21-3

prompt:
    Which describes half-life best?

options:
    {"id":"fall","label":"The time for a group to fall to about half"}
    {"id":"atom","label":"The time one atom takes to be cut in half","note":"Atoms are not cut in half."}
    {"id":"end","label":"The time until nothing is radioactive","note":"Some radioactivity is left after one half-life."}

answer: fall

explanation:
    Half-life is the time it takes for a group of radioactive nuclei to fall to about half.
